{title: Praise to the Lord, the Almighty}
{artist: Joachim Neander · tr. Catherine Winkworth}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 100}

Verse 1
[G]Praise to the Lord, the Al[Em]mighty, the [C]King of cre[D]ation!
[G]O my soul, praise him, for [Em]he is thy [C]health and sal[D]vation!
[G]All ye who hear, now to his [C]temple draw [G]near,
[C]join me in [G]glad ado[D]ra[G]tion!

Verse 2
[G]Praise to the Lord, Who o'er [C]all things so
[G]wondrously reigneth, Shelters thee under His [Em]wings, yea, [C]so gently sustaineth!
[G]Hast thou not seen how thy [C]desires have [G]been
[C]Granted in what [G]He ordaineth

Verse 3
[G]Praise to the Lord, Who hath fearfully, [C]wondrously, made thee;
[G]Health hath vouchsafed and, when heedlessly [Em]falling, hath [C]stayed thee. What
[G]need or grief ever hath failed of [C]relief? Wings [G]of
[C]His mercy did [G]shade thee.

Verse 4
[G]Praise to the Lord, Who doth prosper [C]thy work and
[G]defend thee; Surely His goodness and [Em]mercy here [C]daily attend thee.
[G]Ponder anew what the Almighty can [C]do, If [G]with
[C]His love He [G]befriend thee.

Verse 5
[G]Praise to the Lord, Who, when [C]tempests their warfare
[G]are waging, Who, when the [Em]elements madly around [C]thee are
[G]raging, Biddeth them cease, turneth their [C]fury to [G]peace,
[C]Whirlwinds and [G]waters assuaging.
